  "worked_solution": "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=3f(x)+5,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=3f(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215498/assets/3a214545d208f9ed577c7240f2f025729f9ab8e6354d1a19e8917671de7f5095.png)\n\n- Then, translate it up by $5$ units to get the graph of $y=3f(x)+5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215498/assets/d51fd0e1cc6b05182cca61b97a46970ab456dd9ba2ddebb0ba9c6d197f698a13.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
